{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-275781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y+z=-1 \\\\ x-y+3z=2 \\\\ -2x+y-z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, and the inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 & -8 \\\\ -5 & 0 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe solution of the system of equations is \n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}, \n$\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}, \n$\\,z=$\n{{field-3}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-275781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 & -8 \\\\ -5 & 0 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is \n\n$$\nx=-1,\\,y=0,\\,z=1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-275781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a25c47371cb5ede8ec6ee3fdcdcd7c8a35474135dbd8aff72edb68649a8c7c23"} {"question" "q-275781" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-275781" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-275781" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-275781" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-275781" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-275781" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-78549" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+4z=-2 \\\\ x+3y+9z=0 \\\\ y+6z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n\\,{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}9 & -8 & 6 \\\\ -6 & 6 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-78549" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & -8 & 6 \\\\ -6 & 6 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=0,y=-3,z=1.$\n\nFinally, $x+y+z=0+(-3)+1=-2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-78549" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a25c47371cb5ede8ec6ee3fdcdcd7c8a35474135dbd8aff72edb68649a8c7c23"} {"question" "q-78549" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-78549" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-78549" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-78550" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-3y-2z=-2 \\\\ 5x+y+z=-1 \\\\ -8x+2y+z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n\\,{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -13 & -15 & -11 \\\\ 18 & 22 & 16\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-78550" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -8 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -13 & -15 & -11 \\\\ 18 & 22 & 16\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=0,y=4,z=-5.$\n\nFinally, $x+y+z=0+4+(-5)=-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-78550" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a25c47371cb5ede8ec6ee3fdcdcd7c8a35474135dbd8aff72edb68649a8c7c23"} {"question" "q-78550" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-78550" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "-5"] ["math" "-9"] ["math" "0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-78550" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-78552" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x-3y+2z=-4 \\\\ -4x+4y-3z=7 \\\\ x-y+z=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n\\,{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-78552" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=1,y=2,z=-1.$\n\nFinally, $x+y+z=1+2+(-1)=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-78552" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a25c47371cb5ede8ec6ee3fdcdcd7c8a35474135dbd8aff72edb68649a8c7c23"} {"question" "q-78552" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-78552" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-78552" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-78557" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y+3z=2 \\\\ x-2y-5z=-1 \\\\ 2x-3y+2z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n\\,{A}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-19 & -7 & 11 \\\\ -12 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-78557" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-19 & -7 & 11 \\\\ -12 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=5,y=3,z=0.$\n\nFinally, $x+y+z=5+3+0=8.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-78557" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a25c47371cb5ede8ec6ee3fdcdcd7c8a35474135dbd8aff72edb68649a8c7c23"} {"question" "q-78557" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-78557" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "5"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-78557" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-104546" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}z+x=2 \\\\ 2y-3z=1 \\\\ 2z-y=-3x+3\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-104546" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We organize the system so that it’s in the correct order first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x+z=2 \\\\ 2y-3z=1 \\\\ 3x-y+2z=3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(4-3)-0+(0-6) \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 9 & -6 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -9 & -6 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -9 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=-\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -9 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -9 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=1,y=2,z=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-104546" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a25c47371cb5ede8ec6ee3fdcdcd7c8a35474135dbd8aff72edb68649a8c7c23"} {"question" "q-104546" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-104546" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-1,y=-1,z=2"] ["math" "x=1,y=-2,z=-1"] ["math" "x=1,y=1,z=2"] ["math" "x=1,y=2,z=1"] ["math" "x=2,y=1,z=1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-104546" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=1,y=2,z=1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-42449" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-3+z=0 \\\\ 5y-1+3x=2z+1 \\\\ 3z+2x-1=2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind  $x+y+z.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-42449" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's rewrite the system in the correct order:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+z=3 \\\\ 3x+5y-2z=2 \\\\ 2x-2y+3z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we  write the system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|-0+|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(15-4)+(-6-10) \\\\  & =22-16 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}11 & 13 & -16 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -4 \\\\ -5 & -7 & 10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}11 & -13 & -16 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 4 \\\\ -5 & 7 & 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}11 & -2 & -5 \\\\ -13 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -16 & 4 & 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}11 & -2 & -5 \\\\ -13 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -16 & 4 & 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to the given system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}11 & -2 & -5 \\\\ -13 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -16 & 4 & 10\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ -24 \\\\ -30\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $x+y+z=4-4-5=-5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-42449" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a25c47371cb5ede8ec6ee3fdcdcd7c8a35474135dbd8aff72edb68649a8c7c23"} {"question" "q-42449" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-42449" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-5"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "10"] ["math" "13"] ["math" "3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-42449" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-9722" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2y+3z+x=-1 \\\\ 4z+y=1 \\\\ 5x+6y-3=-3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-9722" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We organize the system so that it’s in the correct order first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+3z=-1 \\\\ y+4z=1 \\\\ 5x+6y=0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(-24)-2(-20)+3(-5) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-24 & -20 & -5 \\\\ -18 & -15 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-24 & 20 & -5 \\\\ 18 & -15 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -4 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-24 & 18 & 5 \\\\ 20 & -15 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{1}[\\begin{aligned}-24 & 18 & 5 \\\\ 20 & -15 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-24 & 18 & 5 \\\\ 20 & -15 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}42 \\\\ -35 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=42,y=-35,z=9.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-9722" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a25c47371cb5ede8ec6ee3fdcdcd7c8a35474135dbd8aff72edb68649a8c7c23"} {"question" "q-9722" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-9722" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-42,y=-35,z=9"] ["math" "x=22,y=-45,z=-9"] ["math" "x=42,y=-35,z=-9"] ["math" "x=42,y=-35,z=9"] ["math" "x=42,y=35,z=9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-9722" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=42,y=-35,z=9"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-275787" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+z=4x+y+2 \\\\ x+y=2z+2 \\\\ y=x-y+z+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution $x=[x,y,z]^{T}$ of the system by computing the inverse of the coefficient matrix.\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-275787" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's rewrite the system in the correct order:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3x-y+z=2 \\\\ x+y-2z=2 \\\\ -x+2y-z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we  write the system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|-(-1)|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3(-1+4)+(-1-2)+(2+1) \\\\  & =-9-3+3 \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -5 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=-\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to the given system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-275787" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a25c47371cb5ede8ec6ee3fdcdcd7c8a35474135dbd8aff72edb68649a8c7c23"} {"question" "q-275787" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-275787" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995994/state.json" "file_sha256" "b065f9972521b589059d85837013f478d516446f49d5b266bdbd017a28cd5896"} {"question" "q-275787" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" 